luajit FFI wrappers of native libraries. Must be a thin layer over the
libraries. It is preferable that these are cross-platform. Platform-specific
wrappers must be put in the windows/linux/macos/(other) folders.

Wrappers can implement some metatables, but the API must be as close as
possible to the original library (unless the wrapper implements cross-compat
between linux and windows libraries which have nothing in common).

Libraries must be named the same as the .so/.dll file they correspond to - for
example, libsodium.so becomes libsodium.lua.
